In article <1992Feb27.213156.10154@newshub.sdsu.edu>, add@newshub.sdsu.edu (James D. Murray) writes:

> I personally do not venture into Hell, without AC of atleast -20.
> Minotaurs can make mincemeat of you, if you have low AC.

I just finished a game in which my goal was to be weak and still ascend.
My armor class was only 0.  Minotaurs ARE a real pain, but if you can teleport
at will you don't ever need to stick around and be killed.  (There are only
a few levels on which you can't teleport.)  


>   You can also try to use magic markers to write scrolls of enchant armour 
>   on blank scrolls.  This is a more difficult option, as it does not work 
>   most of the time. You might end up with some other scroll (like identify 
>   etc.)

Writing a blank scroll with a magic marker will always yield the specified
scroll if you spell the type of scroll correctly and you've already discovered
the type of scroll you're trying to create.  

You can also get a high AC if you have polymorph control and some way of
polymorphing.  (There are usually MANY polymorph traps in hell.)  Some
monsters have pretty darn low AC, and some of these can even wear your 
armor to further lower AC.

